ers -- to reveal a much darker childhood than has been known, a secret affair, and the last chapter of her passionate romance with the Brazilian modernist designer Lota de Macedo Soares. These elements of Bishop's life, along with her friendships with poets Marianne Moore and Robert Lowell, are brought to life with novelistic intensity.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-elizabeth-bishop-a-miracle-for-breakfast-megan-marshall.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.205,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"biographical","score":0.9,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"life of\"","catalog text contains \"family\"","biography subject or topic","biography award category"]},{"id":"character_driven","score":0.4,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"life of\"","catalog text contains \"family\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Elizabeth Bishop","confidence":0.92}],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":false,"statement":"","confidence":0},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.35},"profileConfidence":0.62,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Lota de Macedo Soares","confidence":0.4}],"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Key West","confidence":0.6},{"name":"Brazil","confidence":0.45}]},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"6f2013bcbe3c6b2a39239324bfa1fa0e7ea06afb87a3a93bc97aab2ce3aafada","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Biography","secondarySubjects":["Gender & Sexuality","Arts & Criticism"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book is a detailed life story of poet Elizabeth Bishop, emphasizing her personal experiences, relationships, and contributions to poetry.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"699210e47d2cb4dac283bbcace75634f9fc25f4c1f3d65efbd4e503e2eede16c","displaySummary":"Since her